= Liquidity provider — Technical =

LP returns decompose into fee income, inventory rebalancing effects, asset-price exposure, opportunity cost, and protocol-specific incentives/costs. In range-based AMMs, active liquidity and fee earning depend on whether the market price lies inside the provider's chosen interval.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* liquidity provider ≠ trader by identity
* liquidity provision ≠ risk-free yield
* fees ≠ guaranteed compensation for losses

== References ==
* BIS Working Paper 1227, “Decentralised dealers? Examining liquidity provision in decentralised exchanges” (2024).
* BIS, “Trading in the DeFi era: automated market-maker” (2021).
* Uniswap v3 Core whitepaper (2021), for concentrated-liquidity implementation mechanics.
